From 4b49a767d36291016da99ff9ec08d94ff9bf8c7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Watson <dre@ligandal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:11:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/32] perf(mxfp8): SM120 skinny MXFP8 GEMM on native
 block-scaled MMA, opt-in

SGLANG_SM120_MXFP8_SKINNY=1 routes MXFP8 dense linears (use_mxfp8, M<=32, no bias)
on SM12x to a Triton tl.dot_scaled kernel that quantizes activations in-kernel
with flashinfer mxfp8_quantize's rule (2^ceil(log2(amax/448)), RNE-sat e4m3;
measured 100% match) and reads weight + linear ue8m0 scales once. Replaces
FlashInfer CUTLASS mm_mxfp8 + its separate quantize launch, which run at
45-55% of DRAM bandwidth at decode M on SM120 (slower than BF16 cuBLAS).
GPU2, arbitrary tensors, N scaled to the RTX PRO 6000's per-SM work:
1.7-1.95x vs CUTLASS on in_proj/qkv at M<=8, 1.3-1.6x on o_proj/shared/indexer;
output matches CUTLASS within 1 bf16 ulp; graph replay on two streams correct.
